From e6373b4e9ec971fc8434febd07b53d52ffd842a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:53:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a display that is back on a scrambled HDMI
 link of nvidia-drm has the output set up again

Above a TMDS character rate of 340 MHz the source scrambles the HDMI link
and tells the sink so through its SCDC registers. A TV that is switched off
and on resets them and gives a hot-plug pulse; until the source writes them
again it cannot read the link. i915 reads them at each hot-plug event and
sets the link up again where the sink lost them (intel_hdmi_reset_link()),
amdgpu does a commit for a sink that it saw leave. NVKMS writes them only when
it sets a head up, in the closed part of the driver, and its open part cannot
read them: after the pulse nvidia-drm sends the event and reads the same
EDID, and nothing more happens.

Issue #11: RTX 3050, LG B7 on HDMI-A-3, 3840x2160 at 50 Hz (594 MHz,
scrambled). After the TV was switched off and on there was no picture; Kodi
logged "Modes: after a hot-plug event the display of HDMI-A-3 has the EDID that
the resolutions were made with: nothing is done", the kernel's log and the DRM
state were the same before and after, and a change to 1080p (not scrambled)
brought the picture back.

Now, on nvidia-drm, a hot-plug event after which the display in use is there,
on a connector that drives it as HDMI (an HDMI one, or a dual-mode DisplayPort
one with NV_DUAL_MODE_TMDS 1), with the output on in a mode whose link is
scrambled (pixel clock at the depth that NV_OUTPUT_BPC says, 8 bits otherwise,
above 340 MHz), has the output turned off and on again once, as when the screen
is blanked and woken: NVKMS sets the head and the link up from scratch, SCDC
included. It is looked at 2 s after the last event of a burst, from the frame
path (a video that plays included: the TV was off). The open part of the
driver cannot tell whether the sink lost the setup, so a picture that was there
goes black for the time the TV takes to sync again, once, right after the
event. Nothing is done:

- at 340 MHz or less, on i915 and amdgpu, with the output off, or while native
  Dolby Vision is on (leaving it turns the output off and on or sets the mode
  of the menus, which sets the link up again);
- where another output of the device changed (connected, disconnected, another
  EDID) and the one in use did not: the event is that output's;
- for an event within 10 s of the output turned off and on for this (the
  sink's answer to it), nor twice within 30 s.

A refusal to turn it off leaves it as it was; one to turn it on again is asked
again with the frames after it, as after a flip that did not come
(OutputLeftOff(), FlipOutputOn()). <video><hotplugrelink>false</hotplugrelink>
</video> in advancedsettings.xml turns it off. kodi.log says each case, at INFO
where a display may stay without a picture ("Hot-plug: the display of HDMI-A-3
is there again after the event, with the output on in 3840x2160 @ 50 Hz, whose
HDMI link is scrambled (TMDS 594000 kHz at 8 bpc): the output is turned off and
on again once ..."), at DEBUG otherwise.

The decision is in HotplugRelink.h, without DRM, for a host test.
